  "The Pole Draws from the Vein (d8) is a passive art: a technique Effect on the Pivot canon, not an art record; it takes no slot and never fires (pending word technique-effects attaches it).",
  "The Pole Draws unlocks at layer 4, not 7: d8's own holder list (six people) holds the canon at layers 4-6.",
  "The Dipper Handle is paced, one star a breath: a second Metal art within 1 s moves no star, a non-Metal damaging art loses the count, and recovery comes after 3 s with no damaging art. As written, the always-fire sim lost the count about 10 times a fight and the handle pointed about 0.1 times.",
  "The Pivot's still stance is a self-state counter, not a stance slot, so it never overwrites Mountain Stance in the same kit.",
  "A 'Weight' is an Earth debuff stack on the foe (the Pivot canon's own definition); Weighed lays one and Sentence Stands reads it.",
  "'Your ward' is your main ward (ward_pct), which every fighter holds; The Door Stays Shut grows the stance ward, which ward_grow creates if none exists.",
  "'Breaks the foe's ward' is Exposed (an existing curse), not a new break_ward word: an existing word that keeps the intent wins; 'ignores the ward' on a hit is bypass 0.5, as in Băng Tâm.",
  "'Strike nothing' or 'wait' is the Composed clock (own.since_act): companions, summons and the basic attack do not break it.",
  "Signature items: base common art or ward with the R6 exception on weapons and body gear; all unique.",
  "Treasures keep kind treasure and get rarity 5 (grade + 1) for lint_items; the tally gets base phu; the spears stay on phi_kiem as the depth note says.",
  "Stand-ins: the 5 Earth-rooted servants take the Weighing-Stone Primer (its text admits a one-element root); the 3 Water and Wood servants take a new method, Water-Clock Breathing (the seat keeps time by water clock).",
  "Retunes after Băng Tâm's baseline (all under the art lint): Handle cut 2.3, Weigh the Heart 3.0, North Star Writ 1.4, Pivot +4 % per Weight, the Dipper's damage_more 3 [kim], the Pivot trades ward efficiency for linh lực regeneration +16 % (sustain was the elders' bottleneck).",
  "Plant the Stele needs a fifth of linh lực in hand, so its rising refund cost cannot drive linh lực below 0; there is no cap on charges.",
  "The Weakest File's 'pierce a fifth of its resistances' is pen 40 scoped to spear arts and companions (the engine's pierce only cuts realm suppression)."
 ],
